The DTC SIFMU Structure:
Designated as a SIFMU under Title VIII of Dodd-Frank (12 U.S.C. § 5463), the Depository Trust Company (DTC) immobilizes over $80 trillion in eligible securities.
Fungible Bulk Immobilization via Cede & Co.:
Securities are registered on issuer corporate books in the legal name of Cede & Co., the partnership nominee for DTC. Physical certificates remain vaulted or recorded electronically via the Fast Automated Securities Transfer (FAST) system with transfer agents.
Legal Architecture of Security Entitlements (UCC Article 8):
Under Uniform Commercial Code (UCC) §§ 8-501 through 8-511, investors hold "Security Entitlements" (a package of economic and procedural rights against their direct broker) rather than direct property titles to specific shares.
SAB 122 Rescission of SAB 121 (Digital Asset Custody):
On January 23, 2025, the SEC issued Staff Accounting Bulletin No. 122, which formally rescinded SAB 121 on a retrospective basis. This removed the requirement for custodial banks to record safeguarded digital assets as on-balance-sheet liabilities, enabling Tier-1 custodians to scale crypto-asset safeguarding services within standard Basel III leverage ratios.
