1. Operational Window Compression & SSI Failures
Reconciliation Window Reduction: Slashes the available post-trade reconciliation window from 12 hours to 2 hours (an 83% reduction).
Affirmation Deadline (9:00 PM ET): Institutional allocations must be submitted by 7:00 PM ET on trade date ($T$), and trade affirmations must be finalized by 9:00 PM ET on $T$.
Night-Cycle Processing (11:30 PM ET): Affirmed trades enter the NSCC CNS Night Cycle at 11:30 PM ET on $T$. Unaffirmed trades fall out of automated CNS processing and must be settled via gross, manual matching on $T+1$.
Standing Settlement Instruction (SSI) Errors: Inaccurate or unverified SSIs represent a primary driver of T+1 settlement failures, as manual data corrections cannot be executed within the 2-hour post-trade window.





